    {
      "id": "cc3efe7f9069887bc7018379b264fddaca1cb50a",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": true,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1733184584,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "This return value is -1 if we couldn't get the exit code from dumpcap. Otherwise, it's a nonnegative exit code from dumpcap, probably not / shouldn't be 0 because dumpcap sent an error message.\n\nIf the dumpcap command to get the stats failed because there are no interfaces, that's not a fairly low priority, but there are other failure conditions that probably do warrant noticed.\n\nWe probably should ensure that dumpcap uses the exit codes in `include/ws_exit_codes.h`, and then handle things differently depending on the exit code. `WS_EXIT_NO_INTERFACES` is not worth a console warning at default priority but some of the others might be.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
